From: Claude (Anthropic AI) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 6 Sep 2026 11:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vkd3d: Resolve OMM handles for prebuild sizing too.

The EXT opacity micromap linkage converter leaves micromap == VK_NULL_HANDLE
and defers resolution to vkd3d_acceleration_structure_resolve_omm_va_maps_ext,
which is called from exactly one place: the command recording path. The size
query in d3d12_device_GetRaytracingAccelerationStructurePrebuildInfo never
calls it.

usageCountsCount is zero on both paths by default, deliberately, so that the
two cannot disagree about the histogram. That leaves the linkage handle as the
only channel by which the driver can learn a BLAS carries micromaps at all --
and it disagrees: NULL when the application asks how much memory to allocate,
live when the build actually runs. ResultDataMaxSizeInBytes and
ScratchDataSizeInBytes come back short by the whole micromap overhead, the
application allocates exactly that, and vkCmdBuildAccelerationStructuresKHR
writes past the end of its own suballocation into whatever shares the RTAS
heap. The corrupted BVH then faults during traversal some seconds later, with
no error reported in between.

Observed as VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST while Cyberpunk 2077 streams in the world,
94 occurrences in one run, ~4.4s after the last micromap build and with no
vkd3d error or warning between the two. Runs that touched micromaps on only
two threads did not crash; runs that touched them on eight or nine did.

KHR does not have this problem, because there the micromap is itself an
acceleration structure whose size the driver can read at query time, which is
why the KHR backend can legitimately pass VK_NULL_HANDLE here. The EXT object
is not introspectable while sizing. The upstream EXT backend that shipped for
three years resolved the handle inside the converter for exactly this reason;
its comment said so out loud: "For prebuild info, we need the pointers right
away however." This fallback took the deferred-resolve shape from the KHR
rewrite and lost that property.

Sizing is made best effort: an unresolvable VA there costs accuracy for one
geometry, whereas failing the query outright would report the size of a BLAS
with no micromaps, which is the very undersizing being fixed. Recording stays
hard. Overshooting is harmless -- the application may allocate more than it
needs -- so the only dangerous direction is closed.

Authored by Claude (Anthropic AI) at the request of the repository owner,
from a fleet analysis of the device-lost traces.
---
 libs/vkd3d/command.c          |  2 +-
 libs/vkd3d/device.c           | 14 ++++++++++++++
 libs/vkd3d/opacity_micromap.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 libs/vkd3d/vkd3d_private.h    |  3 ++-
 4 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/libs/vkd3d/command.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/command.c
@@ -21903,7 +21903,7 @@
     if (d3d12_device_uses_ext_opacity_micromap(list->device))
     {
         if (!vkd3d_acceleration_structure_resolve_omm_va_maps_ext(list->device, &desc->Inputs,
-                omm_triangles_infos.ext))
+                omm_triangles_infos.ext, false))
             return;
     }
     else if (!vkd3d_acceleration_structure_resolve_omm_va_maps(list->device, &desc->Inputs,
--- a/libs/vkd3d/device.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/device.c
@@ -9105,6 +9105,20 @@
         goto cleanup;
     }
 
+    /* VK_EXT_opacity_micromap cannot tell a size query that a BLAS carries micromaps by any route
+     * other than the linkage handle: usageCounts is empty by default and VkMicromapEXT is not
+     * introspectable while sizing. Leaving micromap == VK_NULL_HANDLE here therefore answers for a
+     * BLAS with no micromaps at all, while command recording resolves a live handle and needs more
+     * room -- and the application allocates from this query, so the build then runs off the end of
+     * its own suballocation. Resolve here too, best effort, so both size queries see the same
+     * chain. The KHR linkage carries its size in the micromap acceleration structure itself and
+     * does not need this, hence the backend gate. */
+    if (d3d12_device_uses_ext_opacity_micromap(device))
+    {
+        vkd3d_acceleration_structure_resolve_omm_va_maps_ext(device, desc,
+                omm_triangles_infos.ext, true);
+    }
+
     if (build_info.type == VK_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_TYPE_BOTTOM_LEVEL_KHR &&
         VKD3D_CONFIG_FLAG_IS_SET(RTAS_ALLOW_BLAS_REBUILD_SIZES))
     {
--- a/libs/vkd3d/opacity_micromap.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/opacity_micromap.c
@@ -703,7 +703,8 @@
 
 bool vkd3d_acceleration_structure_resolve_omm_va_maps_ext(struct d3d12_device *device,
         const D3D12_BUILD_RAYTRACING_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_INPUTS *desc,
-        VkAccelerationStructureTrianglesOpacityMicromapEXT *omm_triangles_infos)
+        VkAccelerationStructureTrianglesOpacityMicromapEXT *omm_triangles_infos,
+        bool best_effort)
 {
     const D3D12_RAYTRACING_GEOMETRY_DESC *geom_desc;
     D3D12_GPU_VIRTUAL_ADDRESS va;
@@ -729,7 +730,15 @@
         omm_triangles_infos[i].micromap = vkd3d_va_map_place_opacity_micromap_ext(
                 &device->memory_allocator.va_map, device, va);
         if (omm_triangles_infos[i].micromap == VK_NULL_HANDLE)
-            return false;
+        {
+            /* Size queries must keep going. A VA we cannot place yet only costs accuracy for that
+             * one geometry, whereas bailing out would answer for a BLAS with no micromaps at all,
+             * which is the very undersizing this resolve exists to prevent. Command recording has
+             * no such excuse and stays hard. */
+            if (!best_effort)
+                return false;
+            WARN("Failed to place OMM at VA %"PRIx64" while sizing; result may be undersized.\n", va);
+        }
     }
 
     return true;
--- a/libs/vkd3d/vkd3d_private.h
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/vkd3d_private.h
@@ -7133,7 +7133,8 @@
         VkAccelerationStructureTrianglesOpacityMicromapKHR *omm_triangles_infos);
 bool vkd3d_acceleration_structure_resolve_omm_va_maps_ext(struct d3d12_device *device,
         const D3D12_BUILD_RAYTRACING_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_INPUTS *desc,
-        VkAccelerationStructureTrianglesOpacityMicromapEXT *omm_triangles_infos);
+        VkAccelerationStructureTrianglesOpacityMicromapEXT *omm_triangles_infos,
+        bool best_effort);
 void vkd3d_acceleration_structure_flush_postbuild_batch(struct d3d12_command_list *list,
         const struct vk_acceleration_structure_postbuild_info *infos, size_t count);
 void vkd3d_acceleration_structure_write_postbuild_info(
